        <body>
            <div xml:id="d419">

                <pb facs="0635" n="547" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg547"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hirsch to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-03-26"><hi rendition="#italic">March 26, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received April 7.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 413.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a
                    letter from the Rev. H. O. Dwight, dated March 24 instant, stating that a Mr.
                    Bartlett, an American citizen residing at Smyrna, had been denied by the Turkish
                    authorities the right to complete the purchase of his dwelling-house property
                    unless he signed a bond never to allow anything “like” a church or school to be
                    erected on the land.</p>
                <p>Inasmuch as an American has the undoubted right to purchase land in Turkey and
                    build thereon without having illegal conditions imposed on him, I have
                    telegraphically instructed the consul at Smyrna, through the consulate-general
                    here, to send to this legation as soon as possible all the facts and papers
                    bearing on the case.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Solomon Hirsch.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d419-a1.xml" xpointer="d419-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
